        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1058">

                <pb facs="0975" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/552</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bernstorff</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">German Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-29">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 29, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Translation]</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">J. No. A 1883]</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: It has come to my
                    knowledge that a Japanese warship which is lying off the harbor of Honolulu had
                    communication with the land on the 24th and 26th instant. I should be thankful
                    to your excellency for the favor of an explanation of the particulars of and
                    reasons for these occurrences.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Imperial Ambassador: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Prince Hatzfeldt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
